A customer buys the 2.50 Chips with a 20.00 note, but the machine holds only 5.00 in change. Trace the ChangeUnavailableException path: what is the machine's condition afterwards, and was the item dispensed?,"Item dispensed, machine left in DispensingState","Nothing dispensed. resetTransaction() clears the pending purchase and the machine is put back into IdleState before the exception is thrown, so the next customer starts clean","Nothing dispensed, but the pending purchase is kept so the customer can add more money",Item dispensed and the change owed is recorded for later,,2,The failure path deliberately restores the machine to a usable condition before throwing. Leaving it stuck mid-purchase would make one failed transaction take the machine out of service.,1

Real code:

public Transaction insertPayment(double amount, PaymentMethod method) {
    IPaymentStrategy strategy = paymentStrategyFactory.getStrategy(method);

    double credited = strategy.process(amount);

    machine.insertPayment(credited);

    Slot slot = machine.getPendingPurchase().getSlot();
    if (machine.getPendingPurchase().getAmountReceived() >= slot.getPrice()) {
        return completePurchase(method);
    }
    return null;
}

// how Main copes with the return value
private static void printIfCompleted(VendingMachineFacade facade, Transaction transaction) {
    if (transaction != null) {
        System.out.println("purchase complete: " + transaction.getProductName() + ...);
    } else {
        System.out.println("payment incomplete, amount still owed: " + facade.getAmountOwed());
    }
}

insertPayment() returns a Transaction when the purchase completes and null when more money is still owed. What is the practical downside of signalling it this way?,None - returning null is the standard way to signal this in Java,"null carries no information about WHY there is no transaction, and nothing forces the caller to check. A caller who forgets gets a NullPointerException at some unrelated later line instead of a clear message",It prevents the method from ever completing a purchase,It makes the method slower because null must be boxed,,2,"Main happens to check, but only because whoever wrote Main knew to. Returning a small result object, or an Optional, would make 'not finished yet' a state the caller has to acknowledge rather than one they can walk past.",2

