public double getAmountOwed() {
    return machine.getPendingPurchase().getAmountOwed();
}

// VendingMachine
public void resetTransaction() {
    this.pendingPurchase = null;
}

getAmountOwed() is public and can be called at any time. What happens if it is called when no purchase is in progress - for example right after a completed sale?,"It returns 0.0, which is correct","getPendingPurchase() returns null after resetTransaction(), so this throws a NullPointerException",It returns the amount owed on the previous purchase,It throws InvalidMachineStateException,,2,"Main only ever calls it in the branch where a purchase is known to be in progress, so the bug never fires today - it is a latent one waiting for the first caller who does not know that rule.",2

