completePurchase() is private, while selectProduct(), insertPayment() and cancel() are public. What would be lost by making completePurchase() public?,Nothing - more public methods make a class more useful,It is only ever valid to run after enough money has been received

Real code:

public class VendingMachineFacade {

    private final VendingMachine machine;
    private final PaymentStrategyFactory paymentStrategyFactory;
    private final TransactionManager transactionManager;

    public VendingMachineFacade(TransactionManager transactionManager) {
        this.machine = VendingMachine.getInstance();
        this.paymentStrategyFactory = new PaymentStrategyFactory();
        this.transactionManager = transactionManager;
    }
}

The facade needs three collaborators. One is passed in, the other two it obtains itself. Why does that inconsistency matter?,"It does not matter, since all three end up in final fields","Only the passed-in one can be swapped by the caller. The machine and the factory are fixed at compile time, so a test or a second configuration can replace the transaction manager but not the other two",It matters only because the constructor is public,It prevents the class from being used more than once,,2,"Nothing is wrong with a class creating a small stateless helper such as the factory. The machine is the questionable one, because it is the collaborator most likely to need swapping.",2

Real code:

