The requirement said the outside caller should never need to coordinate slot lookup, payment validation, change calculation and stock decrement itself. Which single sentence best describes what this method is therefore responsible for?,Implementing the payment rules for each payment type,Ordering other objects' work correctly and handling the failure path - it performs almost no calculation of its own beyond computing the change amount,Storing the machine's slots and change reserve,Deciding which condition each state class should transition to next,,2,"A good facade is mostly a sequence of delegations. If it starts accumulating rules of its own - a card minimum here, a fee there - it has stopped being a facade and become a second home for business logic.",1

Real code:

public Transaction insertPayment(double amount, PaymentMethod method) {
    IPaymentStrategy strategy = paymentStrategyFactory.getStrategy(method);

    double credited = strategy.process(amount);

    machine.insertPayment(credited);

    Slot slot = machine.getPendingPurchase().getSlot();
    if (machine.getPendingPurchase().getAmountReceived() >= slot.getPrice()) {
        return completePurchase(method);
    }
    return null;
}

A new requirement arrives: refund the customer if they cancel after paying partially. Based on how responsibilities are currently split, where should the money movement live?,"Inside AwaitingPaymentState.cancel(), because that is where cancel is handled","In the facade, because moving money means coordinating the change reserve, the pending purchase and the machine condition together - which is the same multi-step job completePurchase() already does","Inside PendingPurchase, because it holds the amount received","Inside ChangeService, because it owns the reserve",,2,"The state class can decide that a cancel is legal and what condition follows, but the moment several collaborators must be updated in order, that sequencing belongs where the other sequences live.",2

