public static void main(String[] args) {
    VendingMachine machine = VendingMachine.getInstance();

    machine.addSlot(new Slot("A1", "Chips", 2.50, 3));
    machine.addSlot(new Slot("A2", "Soda", 1.75, 2));
    machine.addSlot(new Slot("A3", "Candy Bar", 6.00, 1));
    machine.receiveCash(50.0);

    TransactionManager transactionManager = new TransactionManager();
    VendingMachineFacade facade = new VendingMachineFacade(transactionManager);

    facade.selectProduct("A1");
    printIfCompleted(facade, facade.insertPayment(3.00, PaymentMethod.CASH));
    ...
}

Reading only Main, how much would a new developer need to know about IMachineState, PendingPurchase, ChangeService or the payment classes to follow what the program does?,All of them - Main names each one directly,"None of them. Main names the machine, slots, the facade, a transaction manager and the payment method enum
